],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"B, 132","reason":"If the fourth pattern is not a pair, it has four possibilities, giving 4·4!=96 assignments. Otherwise one of the three pair patterns repeats, giving 3·(4!/2!)=36 assignments. The total is 96+36=132.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_h234"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2012_AMC_10B_Q24","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"classify-extra-song-pattern","label":"Classify the extra song pattern","methodDirectNodeIds":{"classify-extra-song-pattern":["cnm_h234","math:multiset-permutations"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_h234","math:multiset-permutations"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":2,"alignmentIds":["alignment:ab0f6c0e9c4e83915c96d494"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"B (132)","reason":"If exactly three songs have pair types, choose the exceptional song in 4 ways, its liking subset in 4 ways, and arrange the three required pair types in 3! ways, giving 96. If all four have pair types, choose the repeated type in 3 ways and its two positions in 6 ways, then order the other types in 2 ways, giving 36. Total: 132.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_h234"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2012_AMC_12B_Q16","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"classify-pair-type-multiplicities","label":"Count three or four pair-liked songs","methodDirectNodeIds":{"classify-pair-type-multiplicities":["cnm_h239","cnm_h234"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_h239","cnm_h234"]},{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_h231","cnm_h233","cnm_h237"],"id":"classify-number-of-pair-songs","label":"Method 1: Count three or four songs liked by pairs","methodDirectNodeIds":{"classify-number-of-pair-songs":["cnm_h232","cnm_h239","cnm_h234"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_h232","cnm_h239","cnm_h234","cnm_h231","cnm_h233","cnm_h237"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":2,"alignmentIds":["alignment:ab0f6c0e9c4e